&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anteris® Technologies is a global structural heart company dedicated to revolutionizing cardiac care. With offices in Minneapolis, MN, US; Geneva, Switzerland; and Brisbane and Perth, Australia, we have a growing and inclusive team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to forge new frontiers in cardiac care by pioneering science-driven and measurable advancements to restore heart valve patients to healthy function. Transcatheter Aortic Valve Replacement (TAVR) technologies were originally designed for older, high-risk patients. Today, younger, more active patients need a better solution that will not just open and close but restore healthy heart function. We seek to restore healthy blood flow patterns by creating the world’s first biomimetic TAVR valve, DurAVR® THV. This cutting-edge valve, incorporating our proprietary ADAPT® anti-calcification technology, is designed to mimic the natural function of a healthy heart valve.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;262&quot; data-end=&quot;652&quot;&gt;Anteris Technologies is advancing innovative structural heart technologies designed to redefine expectations in the treatment of aortic stenosis. Our Clinical Affairs team plays a critical role in generating clinical evidence, supporting physicians and clinical sites, and executing global clinical programs that advance our technologies from clinical development through commercialization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;654&quot; data-end=&quot;755&quot;&gt;We are interested in connecting with Clinical Affairs professionals with experience in areas such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;757&quot; data-end=&quot;1411&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;m2l8ey&quot; data-start=&quot;757&quot; data-end=&quot;807&quot;&gt;Clinical trial strategy, planning, and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1m0dygz&quot; data-start=&quot;808&quot; data-end=&quot;861&quot;&gt;Clinical operations and clinical project management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;v0hzzs&quot; data-start=&quot;862&quot; data-end=&quot;903&quot;&gt;Clinical site management and monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1iq5zqt&quot; data-start=&quot;904&quot; data-end=&quot;952&quot;&gt;Field clinical support and physician education&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1xtaqir&quot; data-start=&quot;953&quot; data-end=&quot;1007&quot;&gt;Clinical research and scientific evidence generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;10drdlq&quot; data-start=&quot;1008&quot; data-end=&quot;1060&quot;&gt;Clinical data review, analysis, and interpretation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;3z7dkv&quot; data-start=&quot;1061&quot; data-end=&quot;1110&quot;&gt;Study start-up, site activation, and enrollment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;15qig1z&quot; data-start=&quot;1111&quot; data-end=&quot;1160&quot;&gt;Investigator, KOL, and clinical site engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;v0x1qb&quot; data-start=&quot;1161&quot; data-end=&quot;1208&quot;&gt;CRO, Core Lab, and external vendor management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;r44mdw&quot; data-start=&quot;1209&quot; data-end=&quot;1243&quot;&gt;IDE and pivotal clinical studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1ev6v5&quot; data-start=&quot;1244&quot; data-end=&quot;1302&quot;&gt;Clinical documentation and regulatory submission support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;12qbrbd&quot; data-start=&quot;1303&quot; data-end=&quot;1411&quot;&gt;Cross-functional collaboration with Medical Affairs, Regulatory Affairs, R&amp;amp;D, Quality, and other functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1413&quot; data-end=&quot;1608&quot;&gt;Opportunities within Clinical Affairs may span clinical operations, clinical research, field clinical support, clinical science, and clinical program leadership at a variety of experience levels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1610&quot; data-end=&quot;2009&quot;&gt;Candidates with experience supporting Class III medical devices, structural heart therapies, cardiovascular technologies, catheter-based therapies, or global clinical studies are especially encouraged to apply. Successful candidates are collaborative, adaptable, scientifically curious, and comfortable working in fast-paced environments where strong execution and attention to detail are essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2011&quot; data-end=&quot;2264&quot;&gt;Whether your expertise is at the clinical site, in the field, or leading complex global studies, we invite you to explore opportunities to help generate the evidence and clinical experience needed to bring transformative therapies to patients worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to make a significant impact on the healthcare industry by advancing groundbreaking therapies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and dynamic work environment with a culture of innovation and excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package, including salary, performance-based bonuses, and stock options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career development opportunities and a chance to be part of a growing company that values its employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health and Wellness Offerings:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Dental, and Vision Plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Account (FSA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k + Company Match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life, AD&amp;amp;D, Short Term and Long-Term Disability Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus Plan Eligibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Equity Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Holidays &amp;amp; Vacation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusive Team Environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These evergreen postings are designed to connect us with talented individuals interested in &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;future opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt; at Anteris Technologies. Because openings may vary over time, additional details regarding specific responsibilities, qualifications, work arrangements, and compensation will be shared as candidates move forward in the process for individual roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: We may require proof of COVID-19 vaccination to comply with health institutions, state, local municipality, and/or travel regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Anteris Technologies recruits, employs, trains, compensates, and promotes regardless of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, veteran status, and other protected status as required by applicable law. We have a clear vision: to be a place of belonging for all humans by promoting diversity, multiculturism and inclusion, as a goal and reflection across the organization. Diversity is more than a commitment - it is part of our mission to deliver the best structural heart products on a global scale.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fireblocks is the company bringing global finance onchain. Backed by over $1 billion in capital, we are the premier digital asset infrastructure provider trusted by thousands of industry-defining financial institutions, including banks, payment providers, fintechs, and global corporates such as BNY Mellon, BNP Paribas, ANZ Bank, Western Union, Stripe, and Revolut. Built for institutional scale and security, our enterprise-grade platform and network have powered over $14 trillion in digital asset transfers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sales Engineer, Banking is a technically credible, commercially aware member of the EMEA SE team, responsible for the full technical sales cycle across banking opportunities in Western and Central Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a generalist SE role. You will be expected to engage deeply with treasury operations leads, custody technologists, CISOs, and risk committees inside Tier 1 and Tier 2 banks. You will need to understand how institutional banking technology works — core banking platforms, custody and settlement infrastructure, ISO 20022 and SWIFT messaging, and post-trade workflows — and be able to position Fireblocks clearly within that context.&amp;nbsp;You will work closely with Banking-aligned Sales Directors across your region, taking primary responsibility for technical qualification, PoC delivery, RFP responses, and solution design from first engagement through to onboarding handoff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Pre-Sales&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical qualification for banking opportunities, distinguishing genuine digital asset programmes from exploratory noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver tailored product demonstrations to technical and executive audiences across custody, settlement, treasury, and compliance use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope, design, and deliver Proofs of Concept in bank environments — including navigating infosec review, sandbox provisioning, and API integration testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce and own RFP, RFI, and DDQ responses for banking prospects, maintaining accuracy against Fireblocks&#39; external security and compliance attestations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present Fireblocks&#39; security architecture to CISOs, CROs, risk committees, and product and business line leads with appropriate institutional credibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Design &amp;amp; Client Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate institutional banking requirements — custody flows, settlement logic, treasury management, regulatory reporting — into Fireblocks solution architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with bank technology teams on API integration patterns, core banking middleware, and operational workflow design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-develop technical account plans with Sales Directors, identifying the path from initial engagement to production deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to deal strategy on competitive situations, particularly against technology-first custody competitors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the banking client in internal product and roadmap discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute reusable technical content — solution briefs, reference architectures, PoC templates — that scale across the Banking vertical&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding handoff to Professional Services, ensuring continuity from sales into delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the EMEA SE enablement programme, contributing to banking-specific sessions and peer knowledge transfer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–8 years in a pre-sales, solutions engineering, or technical consulting role, selling into or supporting Tier 1 or Tier 2 banks, financial market infrastructure, or capital markets firms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise sales cycles in regulated financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable track record of scoping and delivering PoCs or technical pilots in bank environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience authoring RFP/RFI responses and engaging with bank procurement, legal, and infosec processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to digital asset, tokenisation, or blockchain initiatives whether from a technology vendor, infrastructure provider, or within a bank&#39;s innovation function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of institutional banking architecture: core banking platforms (Temenos, Finastra, Murex, Calypso or similar), custody infrastructure, or post-trade settlement systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with financial messaging standards: ISO 20022, SWIFT MT/MX, or equivalent settlement and payment protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with API-led integration patterns; able to engage credibly in technical discussions with bank engineering and middleware teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of cryptographic key management concepts, hardware security modules, or MPC/TSS architecture (formal training provided)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of MiCA, DORA, or equivalent EMEA regulatory requirements as they affect digital asset operations in banks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credible with senior institutional stakeholders CISO, CTO, Head of Digital Assets, treasury operations leads, and product and business line owners — not only with technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured, precise communicator: able to write clearly, present confidently, and adapt register for technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially aware: understands deal economics, qualification discipline, and what constitutes productive SE engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed and organised, capable of running multiple active opportunities simultaneously without close supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A European language an advantage&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For employees hired to work from the EU, Fireblocks is required by law to include a reasonable estimate of the compensation range for this role. This range is specific to&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; Germany&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;and takes into consideration a wide range of factors that are reviewed when making a hiring decision, such as years of experience, skills, and other business needs. It is not typical for a candidate to be hired at or near the top of the pay range and each compensation decision is dependent on each individual case. A reasonable base salary range estimate for this position is&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;€80,000 – €110,000. The base salary is one component of the total compensation package, which for some roles may include a target bonus, a very competitive equity grant, and very generous benefits. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;While we believe competitive compensation is a critical aspect of your decision to join us, we do hope you also spend time considering why our mission and culture are right for you. We are creating something transformational here, and we hope you are as excited about the future as we are.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe&amp;nbsp;our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we&amp;nbsp;embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fireblocks.com/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Please see our candidate privacy policy here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fireblocks is the company bringing global finance onchain. Backed by over $1 billion in capital, we are the premier digital asset infrastructure provider trusted by thousands of industry-defining financial institutions, including banks, payment providers, fintechs, and global corporates such as BNY Mellon, BNP Paribas, ANZ Bank, Western Union, Stripe, and Revolut. Built for institutional scale and security, our enterprise-grade platform and network have powered over $14 trillion in digital asset transfers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fireblocks Liechtenstein Ltd. is a payment institution being established to provide Account Information Services (AIS) and Payment Initiation Services (PIS) to institutional clients across the European Economic Area, under authorisation from the Liechtenstein Financial Market Authority (FMA).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director of Operations is a controlling-function role and a member of the Company’s executive management. The role holds primary day-to-day accountability for the sound operation of the licensed entity, acts as the principal local point of contact with the FMA, and provides the substance and operational governance that underpin the Company’s authorisation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role has a defined and focused scope: the Company provides AIS and PIS services, with its technology platform operated by an intra-group technology provider. The Director of Operations is responsible for governing that arrangement and ensuring the entity operates soundly, rather than for building or running technology directly. The role may also support the Fireblocks group’s wider regulated activities where relevant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory and Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary day-to-day point of contact with the FMA for operational matters, managing the ongoing supervisory relationship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the Company operates at all times within the scope and conditions of its authorisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Company’s regulatory reporting obligations and coordinate the annual statutory and regulatory audit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Board and executive management in discharging their governance responsibilities, including preparation and follow-through on Board matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Oversight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold day-to-day accountability for the operational delivery of the Company’s AIS and PIS services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the outsourcing arrangement with the technology provider, including monitoring of service levels, quarterly service reviews, and management of the outsourcing register and sub-outsourcing controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Company’s business continuity and incident management framework, acting as the escalation and decision point in the event of a material disruption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the segregated operational processes that support the Company’s regulatory perimeter, including customer onboarding, support routing, and data governance in coordination with the Risk &amp;amp; Compliance function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk and Control&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Risk &amp;amp; Compliance function to ensure an effective control environment across AML/CFT, operational, ICT, and outsourcing risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the Company meets its obligations under applicable Liechtenstein and EEA regulation, including PSD2/ZDG and, as applicable, DORA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the maintenance of the Company’s risk register and the periodic and permanent control framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial and Financial Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the commercial and financial governance of the entity, including the intra-group service arrangements, in coordination with group finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational sign-off on customer onboarding to the entity, ensuring the dual-entity contracting process is completed and customers are correctly provisioned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Fireblocks group’s wider regulated activities where relevant, bringing operational and regulatory experience to bear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven operational leadership experience within a regulated financial institution — a payment institution, e-money institution, bank, or crypto-asset service provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of the Liechtenstein or wider EEA regulatory environment, ideally including prior involvement in a licence application and ongoing regulator engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A payments background, with an understanding of open banking (AIS/PIS), payment operations, and the associated regulatory obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with outsourcing governance and the operation of a licensed entity that relies on an intra-group or third-party technology provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to the digital asset sector is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Attributes&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The standing and seniority to act credibly as a controlling function before the FMA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgement, personal accountability, and the ability to operate as the responsible individual for a licensed entity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work effectively with a distributed group, including colleagues in other time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fit and proper for a controlling-function role, satisfying the FMA’s suitability assessment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location and Presence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role does not require full-time residence in Liechtenstein. The successful candidate may be resident in Liechtenstein or a neighbouring jurisdiction (Switzerland).The candidate must be willing to travel to Liechtenstein as required and to accommodate periodic working hours aligned with a US-headquartered group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For employees hired to work from the EU, Fireblocks is required by law to include a reasonable estimate of the compensation range for this role. This range is specific to Switzerland and takes into consideration a wide range of factors that are reviewed when making a hiring decision, such as years of experience, skills, and other business needs. It is not typical for a candidate to be hired at or near the top of the pay range and each compensation decision is dependent on each individual case. A reasonable base salary range estimate for this position is&lt;/em&gt; &lt;em&gt;€150,000 – €205,000. The base salary is one component of the total compensation package, which for some roles may include a target bonus, a very competitive equity grant, and very generous benefits.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;While we believe competitive compensation is a critical aspect of your decision to join us, we do hope you also spend time considering why our mission and culture are right for you. We are creating something transformational here, and we hope you are as excited about the future as we are.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe&amp;nbsp;our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we&amp;nbsp;embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
